PARITY NOTES (web -> native)
  • Data: the web `useMap()` is react-leaflet's parent-map handle (NOT an HTTP hook); the
    component is a passive draw controller over the map's persisted `fences`. Native binds
    those fences through the P1/S8 `GeofenceDrawerSource` seam (production wraps the shared
    map holder); no HTTP in the view.
  • Render decision: web `fenceToLayer` (circle when lat/lng/radius present AND radius>0;
    polygon when ring>=3; else nothing) reproduced as `GeofenceGeometry.renderKind` + unit-
    asserted, incl. the circle-wins-when-both precedence.
  • Geometry: web `layerToGeometry` circle/rectangle/polygon ported; the rectangle bounds ->
    4-corner ring [sw,(ne.lat,sw.lng),ne,(sw.lat,ne.lng)] pinned verbatim by a test.
  • describeFence: "{name} — {radius.toFixed(0)}m circle around {lat.toFixed(4)},
    {lng.toFixed(4)}" / "{name} — {N}-vertex polygon" / name — ported with locale-independent
    toFixed parity; the web's hardcoded prose is promoted to P1/S10 keys (the only user-facing
    strings the anonymous web source has).
  • Draw modes: web `GeofenceMode` ('circle'|'polygon'|'rectangle', default ['circle'])
    reproduced; the leaflet-draw click/edit/delete handlers become the GeofenceDraft reducer +
    the model's onCreate/onEdit/onDelete seam.
  • Leaf-state widening: the web controller renders no loading/empty/error of its own; the
    Apple modal-surface contract adds them (skeleton / friendly empty / retryable error) PLUS
    the stale+offline freshness axis. The map + toolbar stay live in the empty + content
    phases so the first fence can always be drawn (documented enhancement, NOT silent drift).
  • Charts/maps: web Leaflet -> MapKit; NO Recharts in the source, so no Swift Charts.

